<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Winter War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Winter War was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> from November 1939 to March 1940, after Finland refused Soviet demands for territory. Finnish forces inflicted heavy losses on the much larger <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow-peace-treaty">Moscow Peace Treaty</a> of March 1940 forced Finland to cede <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vyborg">Viipuri</a>, and other areas, while keeping its independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/winter-war.jpg" alt="Winter War" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Finnish_Maxim_M-32_machine_gun_nest_during_the_Winter_War.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
